WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.051 --> 00:00:01.419
(audience clapping)

00:00:01.419 --> 00:00:03.345
- Oh my god, I was dying

00:00:03.345 --> 00:00:06.305
watching your comedy, you are so funny.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:09.300
I love when comedians take
like real life scenarios

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.080
that we all get and no one talks about,

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.341
and then you use it like that.

00:00:12.341 --> 00:00:13.260
It's so funny.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.910
- Driving kids back and
forth to school every day.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.592
You gotta figure out how
you're gonna survive.

00:00:17.592 --> 00:00:18.890
- Yes.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.510
I try and hang my hand
out, but you're right.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:21.343
Never gonna let me in.

00:00:21.343 --> 00:00:22.176
- No

00:00:22.176 --> 00:00:24.040
- Yeah. They're like,
I've gotta be somewhere.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.060
I'm like, don't we all.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:25.893
- I know.

00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:27.691
- But someone told me that
we almost met years ago.

00:00:27.691 --> 00:00:28.672
- Oh man.

00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:30.171
So I was there when you won

00:00:30.171 --> 00:00:31.800
- American idol

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.611
- American idol with my kids.

00:00:33.611 --> 00:00:35.251
(audience laughs and claps)

00:00:35.251 --> 00:00:37.350
- What? Wait, how old were your kids Then?

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.410
- So they were little.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:39.910
They were, you know, they're
in their early, they're

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.843
in their early twenties
now, but they were little.

00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:42.890
- Wow

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.070
- So you are the person that,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.450
that you belong to me and my daughter.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:51.610
- I will cry right now with
that statement, that's so nice.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.392
- You know, we were going
through, it was a tough time

00:00:55.392 --> 00:01:00.392
and a friend, Kevin, who was
a musical director there.

00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:01.316
- Yeah.

00:01:01.316 --> 00:01:04.030
- Gave me tickets so that
I could take my children

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.139
cause my daughter loved American idol

00:01:06.139 --> 00:01:08.010
and we got to see you win.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:08.843
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.700
That's a weird full circle moment.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.060
Well, awesome not weird.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:14.893
- I know.

00:01:14.893 --> 00:01:16.580
- Okay. Well let's talk
about your comedy special.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.890
So it's called Fighting Words.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.723
- Yes.

00:01:18.723 --> 00:01:19.556
- Which I love.

00:01:19.556 --> 00:01:21.090
Why did you title it that?

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.940
- Well, you know, I took on society

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:24.823
cause I'm really,

00:01:26.472 --> 00:01:29.480
if you say I don't like apples

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:33.530
on the internet, to somebody
that means you hate oranges.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.140
- Yeah. Oh, you can't say anything.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.600
- No, you can't win for losing.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.480
If you speak up against a cause,
you're inserting yourself.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.410
If you don't, you're ignoring it.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.570
So I was like, you know
what I'm tired of this.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.720
I am going in on everybody.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.573
I don't care where you are

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:48.406
- I feel like that's
what comedians do though.

00:01:48.406 --> 00:01:49.239
That's what's funny

00:01:49.239 --> 00:01:50.421
- What we're supposed to do, right.

00:01:50.421 --> 00:01:52.830
Everything has gotten so politicized.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.610
I was like, I wanna bring back

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.453
unity by making fun of everybody.

00:01:56.453 --> 00:01:57.952
(audience claps)

00:01:57.952 --> 00:01:59.970
- I mean, and that's
what I love comedians.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.500
Its like everyone gets made fun of

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.820
and that's and then everybody gets

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.283
to laugh at their own self.

00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:06.133
Yeah, it's it's hard though.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:06.966
- Yeah.

00:02:06.966 --> 00:02:07.861
- I talk about that with friends,

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.541
that we're all on TV and I'm like

00:02:09.541 --> 00:02:12.031
which one of us do you
think will get fired first?

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.221
(audience laughing)

00:02:13.221 --> 00:02:14.581
Oh, I'm like, we get nervous

00:02:14.581 --> 00:02:17.352
cause it's hard when
you're an open person.

00:02:17.352 --> 00:02:19.810
And you're also in the
public eye and it's like

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.840
well I have opinions
too, cause I'm a human.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.490
So like, it's a hard thing to navigate.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.580
- Well, you know, I just,
I have adopted a belief

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.670
that you can invalidate
somebody's struggle

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.221
because it doesn't look like your own.

00:02:33.221 --> 00:02:34.054
- Yeah.

00:02:34.054 --> 00:02:36.250
- Every time I give myself that,

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.421
I have peace because everybody

00:02:38.421 --> 00:02:41.850
is looking at life
through their own window,

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.350
and we just can't go around
monitoring everybody's window.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.190
We have to just say,

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.630
hopefully they can come to a
place where they're reading,

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.600
they're seeking information,

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.930
and having empathy for other people.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.813
You know? I think that keeps me sane.

00:02:56.813 --> 00:02:58.900
- Yeah, me too.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.140
I think that's a cool thing about art too,

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.290
is that we're able to do
that in through music,

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:04.181
comedy, television, like all of it.

00:03:04.181 --> 00:03:06.610
Bombing is hard as a comedian or a singer

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.920
any kind of entertainer
on stage, but you figured

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.380
out a way to make money off of it.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.213
Right?

00:03:11.213 --> 00:03:12.046
- Yeah.

00:03:12.046 --> 00:03:12.879
- I love this.

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:16.750
- So I taped my first comedy show.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.400
Kevin Hart was hosting a
show called One Mic Stand.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.760
When I walked down the
stairs, this woman yelled out

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.590
at the audience, who does
this bitch think she is?

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:32.590
I proceeded to bomb so
bad cause it got to me.

00:03:32.642 --> 00:03:33.475
- Yeah.

00:03:33.475 --> 00:03:35.280
- Then Kevin Hart handled her later

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.930
but I made a shirt that said,

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.720
who does this bitch think she is?

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.063
I turned that acronym,

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:45.180
and now bitch stands for

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.107
being in total control of herself.

00:03:47.107 --> 00:03:48.040
(audience cheers and claps)

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.420
- I love that

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.533
You need to like write a book.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.010
Everything you keep saying I'm like,

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.530
gosh, I would read your book.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.021
I love all your little sayings and things.

00:03:58.021 --> 00:03:58.854
- Thank you.

00:03:58.854 --> 00:03:59.760
- By the way,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.270
did it not occur at one point
to be like, I'm this bitch.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.380
- I know, it took a while.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:08.610
- Yeah. I think I would go to anger first.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:09.471
You were nicer.

00:04:09.471 --> 00:04:10.430
Yeah.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:11.490
- I was broken.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.323
I had bombed.

00:04:12.323 --> 00:04:15.730
I was like, you know, and
then I realized, I was like

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.930
oh I gotta work my way to that place.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.810
When I did I made that
shirt, and then I started

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.640
selling 'em all over the country and just

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.370
encouraging all women
and saying, you know what

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.880
let them question who you are.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:28.713
Just show up.

00:04:28.713 --> 00:04:30.232
Just go girl, just do it, do it.

00:04:30.232 --> 00:04:31.065
(audience claps)

00:04:31.065 --> 00:04:32.190
- Isn't it cool how something negative

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.360
ended up being super
positive like in your life.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.193
I love that.

00:04:35.193 --> 00:04:36.720
I love you so much.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.553
- I love you

00:04:37.553 --> 00:04:39.403
- You're so funny and
awesome in person as well.

00:04:39.403 --> 00:04:41.410
Aida's specialist called Fighting Words.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.500
It's on HBO Max.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.750
Y'all gotta check it out.

